---
source: system/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: "help_output(\"fstrim\")"
---
Discard unused blocks on a mounted filesystem

Usage: fstrim [OPTIONS] [MOUNTPOINT]

Arguments:
  [MOUNTPOINT]  Mountpoint to trim (not used with --all or --fstab)

Options:
  -a, --all                Trim all mounted filesystems that support discard
  -A, --fstab              Trim all mounted filesystems mentioned in /etc/fstab
  -o, --offset <OFFSET>    Byte offset to start trimming from [default: 0]
  -l, --length <LENGTH>    Number of bytes to trim
  -m, --minimum <MINIMUM>  Minimum contiguous free range to discard [default: 0]
  -t, --types <TYPES>      Comma-separated filesystem type filter
  -v, --verbose            Print number of discarded bytes
  -n, --dry-run            Do everything except the actual FITRIM ioctl
  -h, --help               Print help
